        print {$LOG_FH} "                     its maximum, so guarantees that add up to more cannot all be delivered.\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     The maximum is set in whole processing units; reserved capacity and LPARs\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     outside the analysis are not counted. Flagged in the CSV as [POOL_SHORTFALL].\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "  Entitlement and    PowerVM needs 0.05 to 1.00 cores of entitlement per VP. The CSV shows, for\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "  VP count           every profile, a current-cycle pair that meets this rule (rENT_Tactical,\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     rVCPU_Tactical); the check confirms it. A pair that fails is flagged in\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     the CSV as [VP_MISMATCH] and indicates a defect.\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "  PowerHA Roles      Roles of the nodes named by ha_peer, from their workload on the same\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     timestamps. An inferred role is evidence, not proof of PowerHA\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     ownership; an unclear case is unresolved. ha_sizing = standby_share\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     gives a standby a share of its primary's target as a floor under its\n";
        print {$LOG_FH} "                     own workload; after a handover the new active node's reductions are held.\n";
